{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5e6442c507d3761d", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Futures Regulation and Registration Checks", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Before investing in commodity futures, check that the individual and firm are registered.", "question": null, "answer": "Before investing in commodity futures, check that both the person you are dealing with and their firm are registered with the National Futures Association (NFA). The source states that anyone who trades futures with the public or gives advice about futures trading must be registered with the NFA. You can also research and verify information using the CFTC’s SmartCheck resource.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 162}}
{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5e6442c507d3761d", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Futures Regulation and Registration Checks", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Anyone who trades futures with the public or gives advice about futures trading must be registered with the National Futures Association (NFA). Before investing in commodity futures, check that the individual and firm are registered.", "question": "What registration checks should you make before investing in commodity futures, and which agency regulates futures trading?", "answer": "Check that both the individual and the firm are registered with the National Futures Association (NFA). Futures trading is regulated by the Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC), not the SEC.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 220}}
{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5e6442c507d3761d", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Futures Regulation and Registration Checks", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Anyone who trades futures with the public or gives advice about futures trading must be registered with the National Futures Association (NFA).", "question": "Misconception: If a futures professional is registered with the SEC, there is no need to check for NFA registration. Is this correct?", "answer": "No. The source says the SEC does not regulate commodity futures and that anyone who trades futures with the public or gives advice about futures trading must be registered with the NFA. Before investing, check whether the individual and firm are registered.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 238}}
{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d0b84009520ee7d8", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Commodity Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "The CFTC cautions investors to be wary of offers for high yield investment opportunities in futures, options, or foreign exchange, also called forex.", "question": null, "answer": "When considering commodity futures, be cautious of offers promising high yields: the source identifies futures, options, and forex as common areas of fraud. Before investing in commodity futures, check that the person and firm are registered with the National Futures Association (NFA). Research and verify information before engaging an investment professional or purchasing commodities.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 999, "output_tokens": 464}}
{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d0b84009520ee7d8", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Commodity Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Before investing in commodity futures, check that the individual and firm are registered.", "question": "What should you check before investing in commodity futures to help guard against fraud?", "answer": "Check that both the individual and the firm are registered with the National Futures Association (NFA). The source also cautions investors to be wary of offers promising high returns in futures, options, or forex.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 999, "output_tokens": 167}}
{"id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d0b84009520ee7d8", "source_id": "8bc60d9e36a12b33", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/commodities", "topic": "Commodities", "subtopic": "Commodity Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "The CFTC cautions investors to be wary of offers for high yield investment opportunities in futures, options, or foreign exchange, also called forex. These are common areas of fraud.", "question": "Misconception: A promise of high returns from commodity futures is a sign that the offer is safe.", "answer": "A promise of high returns does not establish that an offer is safe. The source warns investors to be wary of high-yield futures offers and recommends checking that the person and firm are registered before investing in commodity futures.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 999, "output_tokens": 198}}
